st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.


Install the complete Debian environment
---------------------------------------
The rice Ansible playbook installs this fork, its build dependencies, fonts,
picom, the jaguar wallpaper, and the other desktop tools. On Debian 12 or newer
(x86_64 or ARM64), run as your desktop user:

    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install -y ansible-core git ca-certificates
    mkdir -p ~/.local/src ~/.local/share
    git clone https://github.com/crlxs/rice.git ~/.local/src/rice
    cd ~/.local/src/rice
    ansible-playbook -i localhost, setup.yaml --ask-become-pass

Skip the clone if ~/.local/src/rice exists. Run the playbook without sudo; it requests
sudo for system packages. For just the desktop, add --tags suckless.
After logging out and back in, run startx from a local text console. Without
the login environment, use startx "$HOME/.config/x11/xinitrc".
Full documentation: https://github.com/crlxs/rice#readme

The installer clones this fork into ~/.local/src/st and preserves existing
clones and config.h. If this checkout is elsewhere, it remains separate from
the installer's checkout. To use updated defaults in an existing installation,
review local changes, update its source checkout, back up config.h, remove it,
and rebuild so make copies config.def.h. New clones use the tracked defaults.

Publish source and config.def.h changes with git commit and git push. The local
config.h, compiled binaries, object files and backups are ignored. Installation
never publishes changes automatically. Save your work and restart the X session
after changing dwm; newly launched st and dmenu use their rebuilt settings.

Fork appearance defaults
------------------------
The tracked config.def.h owns this fork's visual defaults. A fresh build copies
it to config.h; an existing config.h is preserved. Edit both when changing your
current installation and the defaults for future clones. Commit config.def.h
when publishing settings; config.h is a local build configuration.

Uses Noto Sans Mono and a muted Kanagawa Dragon palette. On Debian install
fonts-noto-mono and fonts-noto-color-emoji. The rice installer also installs
Symbols Nerd Font Mono for Neovim icons and configures font fallbacks.

Text is 14 pixels with 6 pixels of internal padding and a steady cursor.
The default alpha stays at 1; dwm controls whole-window transparency.

Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
your ~/.local namespace by default).

Afterwards build and install st as your desktop user:

    mkdir -p "$HOME/.local/share/terminfo"
    make clean
    make install PREFIX="$HOME/.local" TERMINFO="$HOME/.local/share/terminfo"


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

